s us on the Quran that these actions are for our benefit, for our guidance (alsra17:7) These prayers and good deeds that we're doing, all of this is for our guidance", "It is not for Allah's benefit, He explicitly tells us that He doesn't need it from us So there is no need and there is no demand And I'll put this as a question for anyone who has any common sense or rationality If God \"needs\", and like he says \"constant needs for glorification\" If He needs our glorification, then why does Allah not tell us to worship Him in the Afterlife? Why when the test in this life –which is whether we will obey God or not and worship Him, or we will choose disobedience– When this test is over, why does then Allah not require worship from us?", "Because according to you, He needs our constant worship and glorification! Then why does He just reward us and give us Paradise? Why is there no constant worship in Paradise? Do you see how a simple question like this can refute this idiotic argument? The reason there is no more worship in the Afterlife, because it's no longer necessary for the test Which means the worship was only necessary for the test, had nothing to do with the \"need\", That God needs glorification or whatever All right? Let's see what else he's going to say",))
