#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("Someone can ask the question, \"Or can the jinn harm humans? And are they accountable for that if they choose to harm a human being?\" So, first we need to understand that there are two types of harms that the jinn can cause. One that is visible and one that is hidden. So, for example, a hidden type of harm is that the jinn can eat with you when you're eating, the jinn can eat with you. And then the barakah, the blessing in the food is decreased because the jinn is eating with you. For instance, when you sleep, you know, they can show you nightmares and bad dreams and that is a form of them harming us in a hidden way.", "And there is like an apparent, uh, visible form of harm that they can cause to you. And that can be like, for example, diseases, jinn possession, and things of that sort. If a person enters their house and they do not mention the name of Allah, they don't say Bismillah, the Shaitan can enter with you. And then they can cause corruption. They can cause harm through them entering with you in the house. Now, what's the evidence for that? The evidence for that is the Hadith of the Prophet Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam when he said, \"If a person enters his house and he mentions the name of Allah the Shaitan would say to the rest of the jinn, 'There is no place for you to stay and there is no food.'", "However, if the person does not mention Allah's name, then the Shaitan will say that you have a place to stay. And if he doesn't mention Allah's name when he eats, then the Shaitan will say you have food today. Now, how many jinn enter you? Allah knows best. 1,000 jinn can enter you, 500, 300, 200. You don't know how many of them can enter. And they can go all around the house. They can hide, they stay in the rooms, in the closets, and in the bed under the beds here and there. It doesn't matter, they go in everywhere.", "And they stay in the in the house. Then they start to cause harm. Like what? For example, your wife is there, for example, right? As an example, your wife is there and you say to her, \"Bring me a glass of water.\" Or, \"Can I have a glass of water?\" Then the Shaitan or the jinn whispers to her, what does he say? \"Tell him go get it yourself.\" And then she says, \"Go get it yourself.\" And then an argument starts, a fight starts. They are causing all these types of harms in the house. And the solution is very simple.", "You mention Allah's name when you enter. It's a very simple thing. Same the same thing when it comes to food. You know the Hadith about saying Bismillah so the Shaitan doesn't eat with you. However, there is a specific narration where the Prophet was sitting and was about to eat and the Sahaba were about to eat. And the Sahaba would wait for the Prophet before they eat. For him to say Bismillah, to mention the name of Allah and then eat. And then and this young girl comes, this Jariya comes running and she's about to take from the food so the Prophet holds her hand.", "Then you have this Arabic guy coming as well running and he was about to take from the food so the Prophet holds his hand. And then the Prophet says to the Sahaba because the Sahaba don't see. There is now we're talking about the world of the Jinn is unseen. That the Prophet he says that he in his hand now he's holding the Jinn because the Jinn was trying to do was trying to eat the food using that girl and using that guy. Because Allah's name was not yet mentioned. So the Jinn was trying to join in the food and eat using those people who were trying to hasten to eat before the name of Allah is In his hand now he's holding the hand of the Jinn.", "He's holding the hand of the girl and he's holding with it because imagine the the girl's hand is there and the the hand of the Jinn is right next to it trying to grab from the food and eat. So the Prophet is teaching us this. There is interactions real interactions going on on a day-to-day basis. Entering your house, eating the food, entering the bathroom. The things that you're doing on a day-to-day basis when you are not fortifying and protecting yourself the Jinn have an influence on you in your life. So it's very crucial, very important for us to understand that these of God and the things that we mention and the things that were taught in the Quran and Sunnah are not just mentioned there for the sake of it.", "They're mentioned so we can fortify and protect ourselves from this unseen world which we cannot observe with our own eyes. Someone could say then, okay, what if my young daughter or my young son or whatever enters the house without saying Allah's name? I mean because we know the kids they're not like adults they would know every time before entering the house to mention Allah's name or say Bismillah or say Assalamualaikum or mention Allah. So, you teach your kid if you saw your kid coming in the house without mentioning Allah's name. Take the kid, hold his hand and take him outside the house and say to him say Bismillah or mention Allah's name, say Assalamualaikum and then enter with him.", "So, you can teach him this as a as a habit. And if he goes out and come and says Allah's name, Bismillah, Assalamualaikum and enters, then the jinn will come out. So, it's very important that we do that. So, if you see your son coming, bring them out and bring them in again and teach them that so that can be a part of their life. Similarly, eating food, maybe there's a little girl or a guy coming to eat the food. Before they eat, you say Bismillah, eat a small piece of the food because now you mention Allah's name on the food and then they can eat.", "No problem because Allah's name is now mentioned on the food. Even if they're young and they don't mention, you start and say Bismillah on your own and then they can start eating after you. So, what we need, brothers and sisters, to internalize these ahadith. Need to internalize this understanding. A lot of people complain about being harmed by the jinn or having issues in their life or having but we are not applying the things that protects us. We are not applying the things that are taught in the Quran and Sunnah that fortifies us from these issues.", "It's very important that we understand that. And that's why the Prophet he told Anas ibn Malik, he said to him, \"Ya bunayya, oh young boy or oh my son, if you enter upon your family if you enter your house, fasallim, say Assalamualaikum.\" So, now we took from the hadith before about the shaytan saying to the people to the other jinn, \"Enter.\" We took from it that we say Bismillah or mention Allah's name. And Assalamualaikum, we take from this narration. So, now before you enter your house, say Bismillah, Assalamualaikum and you enter your house. We take this from these two ahadith from the Prophet sallallahu alayhi wasallam.", "Okay. Now, I want to talk about something which is very important which is the idea of mixing between jinn position and psychological illnesses and diseases. It's a very problematic issue that a lot of people do. And I have had even some personal encounters and issues within my family to do things related to that. And I'm going to talk about some of them in a bit, inshallah. However, we got to understand, when you go to people like that do ruqyah or try to help you or or try to help others or you if you are a person yourself doing ruqyah, we need to understand that we need to avoid assumptions because they can cause huge harm and huge issues to be.", "So, for instance, someone goes to a a person who does ruqyah and they are not a qualified person. And they go to them and that you read the Quran or something or someone moves a little bit or whatever, so he starts giving them like a bunch of assumptions. You have this, you have that. That can destroy someone's life. So, it's very important for the person who does it and the person that go to them, you make sure that you go to someone qualified, number one. And whoever is doing ruqyah, that he is sure not to use assumptions.", "But to be certain about the things that he says to the people. Cuz if you say to someone that you have say or whatever, imagine. And then the person he doesn't really have it. Now, everything that happens, he hits, you know, he's walking and he trips, oh, it's because of the say. It's because of hassad, because of this. He loses like his wallet, oh, it's because of hassad, because of say. So, you start causing this form of delusion in the mind of a person that can completely destroy their life. So, it's very important that we use the Quran and Sunnah and double-check and make sure that when we say things to the people, who we go to first and the person who is helping others is using the Quran and Sunnah and is certain of what he's doing rather than misguiding people and confusing them.", "And if you are helping others, don't like just mix like you got to be a qualified person. Not someone who is mixing between what jinn do and between psychological illnesses. Also, another issue is where people they think everything is say, right? Without even going to someone, they think everything is hassad, envy, evil eye, say, jinn possession, They think everything is that. Because they don't want to take accountability. Allah in the Quran tells us, \"Whatever calamity happens to you is because of what your hand have earned.\" And Allah also mentions that some people if a good happens to them, they say it's from Allah.", "If bad happens to them, they say it's from Allah. \"Say it's from yourselves.\" There are some bad things that happen to us that can happen to us in our life. We lose our job, we we get divorced, all of these things. That has nothing to do with hasad. Has nothing to do with evil eye. Has nothing to do with seher. Has nothing to do with jinn possession. Not everything that happens in our life we start saying this is seher. This is This is magic. This is jinn possession. That's why it's very important that we make distinctions and we understand the difference between this and between other things.", "So I I have had like this personal experience in my family like I was saying a close relative. And they would bring all of these people for ruqyah and they will do all sort of things, all sort of like practices that are not based on the Quran and Sunnah. And they would say she has this, she has that, or he has this, he has that, like and all of this stuff. And in the end this was a psychological disorder, let's say a bipolar disorder. Went to a person of knowledge, a person who understands psychological illnesses.", "Just as we believe that the jinn exists and evil eye is true and envy is true and seher is true and magic is true and all of these things we believe in them. At the same time, we don't say that everything is that. So we have to have this middle ground of understanding the difference between the two. Even the doctors. You know, you may come to a doctor who says to you, \"Okay, this is not my specialty. Go to a cardiologist, you know. Go to an abdomen doctor. Go to this.\" He's a doctor and then this is a doctor of the body.", "You could say, \"Okay, do radiation because I just want to make sure. I want to double check.\" So that same idea needs to apply when it comes to this idea of of seher. We need to be sure, double check, and not just say things.",))
#source("Source: The Muslim Lantern, \"How To Protect Yourself From Jinn, Possession, Magic & The Evil Eye In Islam - Muhammed Ali\"")
