#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("So there are types of healers or types of people who do ruqyah. Let's say there's two types. One type is like who just learned from other people. He look at someone who does ruqyah, he did the ruqyah. He watched something and he learned, and he started doing it. And then people started coming to them. And there is another person who studied. He's a alim. He's a person of knowledge. He studied the Quran and Sunnah. What do they say about the world of the jinn? What do they say about their interactions and influences on us? And how do to protect and fortify yourself from the Quran and Sunnah?", "So, if you go to someone to do ruqyah on you, be sure that a person is from the second type, and not the first type of someone who just looked and started practicing and copying other people. It's very important to make sure that you're going to the right people. Some of them will tell you things like the jinn starts to speak, and they say to us, you know, go do that. Start spraying this in the house. Go to that place, you will find this. Go to this place, you will find that. Go to this. Go to that.", "Go to this. And the person who is not a person of knowledge, who had did not learn from the Quran and Sunnah, would listen to the jinn. And would tell you, oh, the jinn is telling us, then this must be true. However, a person of knowledge from the Quran and the Sunnah, you know what he would say? If the jinn, if someone is possessed by a jinn, and you start speaking to them, and the jinn starts to telling you, do this or don't do that, then the person of knowledge will say first, is how are you advising me?", "When you are a sinner. You are a fasq. You're someone who's disobeying Allah and his messenger. Why? Because that jinn is possessing a human being. And it is haram for the jinn. We already said, all of the things in the Sharia, the jinn are also commanded to follow like the the Quran and the prophet. So, harming you by possessing you is haram for that jinn. So, if that jinn is doing something haram already, what makes you think is he's going to start giving you good advice? And he's going to telling you and you should listen to what they say and start applying it.", "So, a person of knowledge will first say to them that first you have to repent. You have to leave this person that you're possessing. You have to repent to Allah before you you start giving me advice. So, a person who is not qualified, like I said, is just a copier. They're like, oh, the jinn the jinn is saying this, then this that must be true. So, it's very important to make these distinctions. Okay, now the question is, how can we be certain if something is jinn possession or if something is just a psychological illness? There are signs.", "What are these signs? You know, the Quran is a healing. If it's being recited on someone, it has an influence on it. There are people who say, \"Oh, I have jinn possession, I have sihr, I have this.\" And Quran is recited day and night and there's no no influences on them. They don't have anything. A person who's possessed by jinn, how can we be sure? Once you recite the Quran on the ruqyah is done on them, they become unconscious. So, that is a sign. First, they become unconscious. And then if they speak, if the jinn speaks, they speak with a different voice.", "They speak with a different voice. It could be a different language even cuz that jinn could be from a different place. So, they speak with a different voice, not your voice. So, if someone says, \"I'm jinn possessed.\" They don't become unconscious. There is no different voice that is being said. They say to you, \"Look, oh, the jinn is speaking. I don't I can't control my voice. I just hear what the jinn is saying.\" That's false. That person is not being possessed by jinn. What if, you know, there's a jinn now and and he starts speaking with a different voice, but he starts giving you advice?", "Start telling you anything anything like let's say he tells you any type of advice. The the the Okay, person who led me to possess you is in this place, is in that place. Do this, do that. The first thing you do is if you hear someone who's being possessed by jinn and the jinn is speaking and is telling you to do something, first thing you do is to Compare it to the Quran and Sunnah. Why? Because the default in what they say is lying. Now, he's a disobedient jinn who's possessing someone. The default in what they say and do is lying.", "We know the hadith where the shaytan tells Abu Hurairah to recite Ayatul Kursi because it's going to be a protection for you before you sleep until you wake up. So, Prophet said, \"Sadaqaka.\" He said the truth wa huwa kadhub. Kadhub means it's from fa'ul that he's an excessive compulsive liar. He lies all the time. So, let's say 90% of what he says, 95% of of what he says is a lie. So, that is our approach with the jinn is that the default of what they say is a lie. So, if what they say is in accordance to the Quran and Sunnah, then we can believe that part.", "However, anything else they say, the default position is that they're lying. The same as the case with Abu Hurairah. He what we what was taken is what the Prophet did takrir of, what he affirmed, which was the recitation of Ayat al-Kursi. So, we accepted that because we compared it to the Quran and Sunnah. However, anything else that's being said is not to be applied. And you'd have a lot of these people who do ruqyah. They come with all types of myths. Some people will tell you to spray salt in the house, and these exist in many cultures, these practices.", "Spray salt in the house and the jinn will not enter. Or like take this amulet or hang this on your wall or say these specific words. And like we said from the hadith before, where did where did you get this information from? It's either you got this This is the world of the unseen. If you believe that spraying salt or doing this or this or that or this amulet or hanging this thing is influencing the jinn, you need What's your source of knowledge? It's either the wahy, you get revelations from the Quran and Sunnah, which we know you don't have, or the jinn told you something.", "And we said the case with the jinn is that the majority of what they say is lying. So, we cannot use personal experiences to apply these things. Most of the those like I'm telling you, the people who do ruqyah who haven't studied the Quran and Sunnah will tell you these They'll say like someone did it and it worked. That's not how we approach the world of the unseen. We approach the world of the unseen using the Quran and the Sunnah. You'll have some of these so-called as well people who do ruqyah. They'll say, \"I'll use a jinn to get another jinn.\"", "So, now imagine a person you are doing ruqyah on them. And then the jinn starts to speak. And he says to you, \"That I can help you. Okay, I repent I can help you. I repent.\" You can You'll ask him, \"How can you help me?\" He says, \"Look, I'm going to start helping you. Whenever you see someone possessed next time, just say say something and I will go into that human being, and then I will start helping you and I'll fight them out. So, a person who like those people who are not experienced from the Quran and the Sunnah, they will say to you uh they will be happy.", "They will like this. However, a person who studied the Quran and the Sunnah understands that this is haram. Because the jinn entering a human being, it's a it's a masia. It's an act of disobedience. So, you would not give permission to the jinn to do something like this. So, when you are well acquainted with the teachings in the Quran and the Sunnah, you don't fall into these issues. And you don't cause harm to others by doing the incorrect wrong practices. Because remember, the healer is Allah, not the jinn. So, you say to that jinn, we have the Quran, we have the book of Allah.", "We don't need you. Don't need you entering anything anywhere. Reciting the book of Allah Azza wa Jal is enough to heal the person that needs healing. It's very very important.",))
