#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("Now, is it permissible, for instance, to recite because we know in the Quran and Sunnah we have things that are specified to recite, like we said before, sleeping at al-Kursi, things that we can do for ruqyah, like, for example, Surat al-Fatiha, or al-Mu'awwidhat, Qul A'udhu bi Rabbil Falaq, Qul A'udhu bi Rabbin Nas, and these uh verses and chapters. However, can we just recite, do we only need to recite these specified verses, or anything from the Quran? The answer is it's permissible to recite anything from the Quran. Allah Azza wa Jalla says, \"Wa nunazzilu minal Qur'ani ma huwa shifa'un wa rahmatun lil mu'minin.\"", "We send down from the Quran what is healing. So, the Quran, all of it is a book of healing. And Aisha, Allah be pleased with her, there was this narration, Abu Bakr entered upon her, and she was doing ruqyah, so he said to her, \"Erqiha bi kitabillah.\" Do ruqyah on her with the book of Allah. So, it is permissible. However, what is not permissible is where you get certain people who say these specific say these specific number of verses, or these specific verses in this specific order, in this specific time, in this specific way. It's permissible for you to do, but it's not permissible for you to make it like it's some form of legislation and start advising people to do this specifically.", "And remember, it is not based on your personal experiences. You cannot say, \"I recited this specific set of verses in this specific set of way, therefore it works, therefore you need to recite it as well.\" The world of the unseen is dependent on the Quran and the Sunnah and what Allah and the messenger tells us. Now, we get to this question. What do you do if you feel you've been affected, because we said you can confuse things. So, what does a person do if they start feeling like they have sehir, like they they have hasad, or they have evil eye, or they have any of these things?", "What do you do? The first thing you need to do is to do ruqyah upon yourself. You do ruqyah upon yourself. Why? Because the messenger that is what he told companion who came to the prophet and he said I find this feeling of pain in my body since I accepted Islam. Then the prophet recommended him to do ruqyah on himself and he said to him say Bismillah three times and say so he said what the prophet commanded him so he said I I said it. So Allah removed that from me. Some of us get this pain get this harm but we don't do this.", "Try it and you will see the effect the influence because that was like pain in his body. So you feel some sort of a pain in your body. And I I have tried this myself. One I I had this pain in my back that I felt that was out of nowhere. And I said this vicar and it was gone. It didn't even take days or whatever. It was gone instantly. So try this. Do it. You use given this revelation so we can apply it to ourselves. So the first thing you do is what? Is you do ruqyah on yourself.", "Now if you do it let's say you do it on yourself a few times and it doesn't work. Is it permissible for you to go to someone else to do it on you? It is permissible for you to go to someone else to do it on you. However it's not going to be the same. Why are we saying do the ruqyah on yourself first? Because you're the one suffering. So you are you will be more humble more in need of Allah when you are calling upon Allah when you're doing the ruqyah. It wouldn't be the same for someone like a stranger who's not you.", "He wouldn't be feeling the same way. And the closer you are to Allah the more humble you are the more dependent you are on Allah the more likely that Allah will answer your prayer. That's why prophet told us that you are the closest to Allah in the state of prostration. You're more humble you're more humiliating yourself you're more coming closer to Allah so you are closer in your sujood because you are in that state. So, it is permissible like if if you try on yourself multiple times it doesn't work, then you go to someone. It is permissible.", "It is not haram. But, it's not recommended because there's a hadith of the Prophet Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam where he said that there's a group of people that will enter paradise without hisab, without accountability before or any punishment. And then he mentioned one of the characteristics of these people la yastaqoon. They don't ask someone else to do ruqyah on them. You can do ruqyah on people, but asking someone to do ruqyah on you will exclude you from being from those group of people. However, it is permissible. Like if someone is in is in case of need and is suffering somehow and tried ruqyah and it's not working, it's just permissible to go.", "However, remember what we said, go to someone who's qualified, someone who's actually studied the Quran and Sunnah, the influences of jinn, how to interact with them, and not just someone who's just been copying other people. There is many people online. Especially in like over I mean I don't want to mention names, but people doing all crazy crazy sorts of things. They put their hand in someone's mouth and crazy things, not from the Quran and Sunnah. And a lot of them are are the majority of them are liars. And people follow them. So, it's very important to be clear on what is from the Quran and Sunnah and what is not from the Quran and Sunnah.",))
