#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("Some others will say to close your eyes. And and look look look what some of these evil people will do. You will go to a person who does ruqyah and be like close your eyes. Then you close your eyes and then you will start seeing that your uncle oh, your uncle is the one who did sihr to you. He put it somewhere in that room and you go and you find something in your closet or something. And then families get separated. I have many stories where I have people saying, \"Oh, my my aunt did sihr on me.", "My this And this is how they know. They go to a person, they close their eye and they see something. The shaytan throws this vision when they close their eyes and they see something and he visualizes something to them so he can cause separation, remember? Allah in the Quran tells us that and you can be in a common with Allah that the shaytan only wants to put enmity and hatred between you and and each other. And Allah tells us that may Allah with his that which separates between the husband and wife. This is what the shaytan wants.", "To separate between you and your wife, separate. Cause enmity between you and other people. We have families that don't speak to to each other for years and years. Oh, this person did sihr to me. This person was the cause of hasad or eye. No proof. They either go to some scam artist that tells them this stuff or they just cause assumptions. This is a very, very evil door that people must be aware from. And you need to be certain using the evidence from the Quran and Sunnah descriptions in the Quran and Sunnah. It's the only way you could be certain that someone did it to you.", "And I can't imagine how many times I can tell you that. People come and they say to me that oh, my family did this to me or that person did this to me. They have no proof for it. So now we ask a question. Is the cure for sihr and hasad and and position, is it different cures or the same cure? Now for for evil eye we talked about the wudu and and washing with wudu. This is mentioned in the nation. However, for hasad, for envy or or magic or position, Ruqyah influences all of these things.", "And of course, the best ruqyah is found in the Quran and Sunnah. Like reciting al-Fatiha, reciting al-Mu'awwidhat, the dhikr that I told you that you that the Prophet told him told the Sahabi to say when he felt pain in his body. All of these things are found in the Quran and the Sunnah, which we're mentioning and we're going to mention more of them. This is how you heal yourself. However, when we say that ruqyah influences all of them, the ruqyah have to be done correctly. Because if you're not doing the ruqyah correctly, a lot of people do ruqyah, but they say, \"Oh, I did ruqyah.\"", "You know, I have I don't know how many times I could say this. Probably if I had the penny for each time someone said I had did ruqyah and nothing happened, I'd probably be rich. But are you doing the ruqyah correctly or not? So, the question is this, how do we do ruqyah the right way? How to do ruqyah correctly? The first thing you need to understand is do you internalize that you're using the Quran as a healing. That you're using the Quran. This is what you're going to use, Quran and the Sunnah, the revelation from Allah to heal yourself.", "The second thing is that you understand that the Quran by itself doesn't heal. Allah is the one who heals. The Quran is a means, is a sabbath for us to heal. The third thing you internalize that you are following the Prophet Muhammad in these practices. Then, you need to know the meaning of the words that you say, the vicar that you say or the dua or the Quran. You need to know the meaning of these things. Because remember, Allah says either Allah want to open on the Egypt and Allah to come up laughing and laugh that ask Allah and you're certain that Allah will answer you because Allah does not accept from a heart that is distracted.", "So, you need to be internalizing, understanding the meaning of the words and your heart is present when you're saying that. And lastly, you need to humble yourself to Allah. Need to feel that you are in need to Allah when you're making this ruqyah. You're asking Allah sincerely to heal the person or to heal yourself from whatever is happening to them. So, a lot a lot of us say things like the of God of the Sabbath and Messiah to protect ourselves. That God of the day and night of God. However, we don't understand their meaning. You need to understand their meaning.", "If you want to protect yourself, you need to understand their meaning. So, I recommend everybody get a book of the explanation of these of Sabah and Masah. Understand their meaning. Think about what you're reading when you're reading it. And if you're used to saying change the orders because if you change the order it doesn't become a habit. Look, so many things when we say a lot becomes a habit and then your mind is not present when you're saying them. But if you change the order you force your mind to think.",))
#source("Source: The Muslim Lantern, \"How To Protect Yourself From Jinn, Possession, Magic & The Evil Eye In Islam - Muhammed Ali\"")

