#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("Now, what is the difference between ain, evil eye, and hasad, envy? Are they the same thing because a lot of people confuse these two things. It's very important for us to understand that they're not the same thing. There's a differentiation between them. So, hasad can only come from an evil soul or evil person that wishes that the ni'mah, that the blessing that Allah has upon you is gone. This is what hasad is. Someone looks at you with the evil that he wishes that whatever good that you have is gone. This is hasad. Evil eye, ain, is that you like something, but you don't mention Allah's name on it, so harm falls on that thing because you don't mention Allah's name on it when you are finding beauty in it or adornment in it or likeness, but you don't mention Allah's name.", "You forget to mention Allah's name or you don't mention Allah's name. The evil eye can happen from a righteous person. It can happen from a father to his son. Can happen from a husband to to his wife. And it is not happening with an evil intent. It's not happening with an evil intent like hasad, but it can happen from a righteous person. And the evidence is that you have the Hadith of Amir ibn Rabi'ah, where he saw one of the other Sahabah, Sahl ibn Hunayf. He was doing iktisal, and he saw his skin and he seen I've never seen beautiful skin.", "So he fell. And then the Prophet said, \"Who are you accusing? Who do you think is the one is the cause of this?\" So they mentioned Amir ibn Rabi'ah. So the Prophet said, why would one of you kill his own brother?\" And here he understand the solution. If someone has an evil eye specifically, what to do. Prophet told him to do wudu, and then to use that water that he used for wudu to pour it on the person who has been affected by ayn. And the Prophet poured it on him, so he recovered. He stood up like nothing happened to him.", "Amir ibn Rabi'ah is from the people of Badr, of the Sahabah from Badr. He's a righteous person. So he affected another person with ayn or evil eye, whatever translation you want to use for it. And he didn't do it with a bad intention. So it can happen from a righteous person, it can happen from you to your own son. So that's very important now that we understand if someone asked me for wudu, someone comes to you and asks me for wudu, that is afraid that you have affected them with evil eye. So they want to ask you for wudu so they can do ghusl with it or wash their body with it so they can make sure that they're no longer affected, is that you don't say, \"How can you come and ask me?", "I'm not an evil person to do envy on your It's not hasad, it's not We're talking about ayn. You could do it when you're not feeling it. You could do it and be from the Sahabah from Badr. It doesn't matter. So do not feel offended if something like this happened. Now, look, something very very important. And this happens to a lot of people, but they don't understand. So, you have Your own baby starts to cry at night. The baby your baby starts to cry. None of the people go and do ruqyah. Recite on him, do some ruqyah.", "It is free. Takes you a few minutes. Try and do ruqyah on your on your son. They go to this doctor and that doctor and and sometimes it doesn't help. Perhaps he's been affected by you or by someone else. So, first do ruqyah. If it doesn't work, you and your wife do wudu and try pour it on that child and see. And go see go and see the doctors if this is not influencing. Go and see the doctors. However, use this in your life because that could be the cause when you are going and trying to find another way of healing.", "And that's why we can fall into abandonment of the Quran. Allah says in the Quran and the messenger said, \"Oh Allah, my people have abandoned this Quran.\" So, the talk about different types of abandonment. The abandonment of The abandonment of actions that we don't do the actions of the Quran and an abandonment of healing. Some people go throughout their entire life and they never do ruqyah on themselves even once. Do it. If you having illness, sickness, disease, feeling headache, feeling something, do this. Make this a part of your life. Allah's revealed to us this because these are acts of worship that we need to implement on ourselves and there is a healing and a barakah and a shifa and a blessing in them.", "So, we need to apply them in our lives. So, how do we protect ourselves like and avoid evil eye and giving someone evil eye or or or this? It's for us to say barakah. So, let's say for example, may Allah give barakah. You say words of barakah. That's what the prophet Some of you say something, then he should ask for barakah upon that thing. Now, some people think that we should say masha Allah and a lot of people say this. They say masha'Allah if they see something they say masha'Allah and they think masha'Allah is how you avoid doing evil eye towards that thing.", "So, asking for baraka versus saying masha'Allah. Masha'Allah is not related to that. That's not the teaching of the prophet. The teaching of the prophet in relation to that, if you see something you like, you ask for baraka. You ask for blessing. You ask for baraka upon that thing. Say Allahumma barik alayhi. Allahumma barik fihi. You ask for baraka. Now, where does the idea of masha'Allah come from? It comes from the Quran. The verse that talks about the garden and one that says to the other only if you enter your garden and you say masha'Allah. There is no power except with Allah.", "There is no power except with Allah. This was the believer speaking to a disbeliever. The person who was entering that garden was a disbeliever. And that's why you see in the Quran in the verses that he says, \"I don't think that the hour will come. I don't think that the day of judgment will come.\" So, that other believer was telling him, \"If only if you enter this paradise, you believed in a creator and you said that this was from Allah. It was with the power of Allah. It's not from my power. It is what Allah willed.\"", "So, he's referring to a specific belief that this was with the power of Allah. What Allah willed is not with my power. This is not in relation that if you see something you like, you say masha'Allah. So, the correct practice is what? If we see something and we want to avoid evil eye or eye or any of that, that we ask for baraka. We say Allahumma barik. For instance, any words of baraka, any words of asking for baraka, you can use and say to avoid evil eye. Now, some people will tell you things like what?", "Looking at mirrors leads you to gym positions or something. Is there evidence from the Quran and Sunnah? No. We know that from the Quran and Sunnah we have narrations that the prophet would look. There is nothing in the Quran and Sunnah that prevents you or or tells you not to look in the mirror or not to look in the mirror for this period of time or not to do that. So, there is no evidence for that. Remember, I told you anything of the unseen must be evidence from the Quran and Sunnah regarding. So, if you would mention Allah's name, say bismillah, mention Allah's name and look.", "However, there isn't anything in the Quran and the Sunnah that says if you look for an extensive period of time. So, be aware of these practices. Some people are like look they close the door of the bathroom, you know. I know so I know some people like that. Close the door of the bathroom because maybe the jinn they're worried about jinn coming out or something. Remember the hadith we just told you. You could enter your house without saying mention Allah's name and the jinn can come in. It's nothing to do with the with the bathroom.", "Plus, you think the door physical door is going to prevent the jinn from coming out? The jinn can be like the wind and they can go through objects. They're for you created from smoke and fire. They can go through under the door. They can go anywhere. Like you closing the door of the bathroom or opening it is not going to change that. You got to be aware of these practices. You get someone who's like is not practicing using the Quran and Sunnah. Oh, I can sense this person has jinn. This person has sihr. Where Where did you get this evidence from?", "It's either a jinn that throws these ideas in your mind and we said they are they're liars or you're claiming to get some revelation. So, whenever sense people if you see people telling you to do all of these myths that I'm telling you, all of these are signs to you that these people are not qualified. They haven't studied the Quran and the Sunnah. I'm giving you all of these examples so you can understand and be able to differentiate if someone family member was possessed or had these issues and they wanted someone to do ruqyah on them that if you hear these things and you hear these recommends oh, put salt here, close the bathroom door, hang this amulet, say this 20 times, do this, do that.", "If you have these people saying these things then you know that that that person is not qualified. So, do not listen to them and find the person who is qualified who uses the Quran and the Sunnah.",))
#source("Source: The Muslim Lantern, \"How To Protect Yourself From Jinn, Possession, Magic & The Evil Eye In Islam - Muhammed Ali\"")

