#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("So, now let's get to an important question. How do I protect myself now from jinn, possession, evil eye and all of these things? How does a person protect himself? The first thing you do is praying in Fajr. You pray Fajr prayer. And a lot of people are going to find difficulty in this. But do you want protection? How you protect yourself. Prophet said whoever prays Fajr he is in the of Allah meaning he is in a protection and the safekeeping and the protection of Allah. Whoever prays Fajr. So, pray Fajr. Second thing is say this this is one of the most powerful you could Say 100 times a day.", "The Prophet will be a protection for him from the jinn until the end of his day. If you say it earlier the best you can protect yourself from the but even if you don't you say it later on so you can protect yourself. It's very very important brothers and sisters. Don't be lazy. Say this. You want to protect yourself this is how you protect yourself. The of the day and night that I was telling you get a book of understanding their meaning and and saying them. You say them after Fajr, after Maghrib. They are day and night reminders and they have words of protection.", "They have statements of protection that protects the person. Until the morning comes. It protects the person until the night comes. If you're suffering, if you're having issues, you see even even if you're not. The people you will see you see the people around you who suffer from jinn or any of these things. You want to be protected this is how you do it. You protect yourself. Also the The praying Jama'ah as a man for the men to pray in Jama'ah, praying congregation. Because the Prophet Alayhi Salaam talking about the Shaitan He said Alaykum will Jama'ah upon you is the Jama'ah fainnama ya'kul al dhib min al ghanam al qasiyah.", "Because the wolf eats from the the lone sheep. The the sheep that has gone away from the rest of the pack. So that Shaitan targets you when you're alone. But in your prayer in Jama'ah is a protection for you. And lastly rely on Allah Azza Wajjal in all your affairs. Have tawakkul reliance on Allah Azza Wajjal. That he's the protector. I understand in my heart Allah Azza Wajjal is the one who protects me. If you do these things and you keep these things by the will of Allah Azza Wajjal you will be protected from anything evil that can happen.", "Okay. So you protect yourself. Now what about your children? How can we protect our children from evil eye or jinn possession or magic or sihr or any of these things? We have a dua that Prophet Alayhi Salaam used as a protection for Hasan and Husayn. His grandchildren. Prophet Sallallahu Alayhi Wasallam would say u'idhukuma bi kalimatillah al tammah min kulli shaytanin wa hammah wa min kulli aynin lammah. What is the meaning of this? Remember, we need to understand the meaning of these words. If you want to be protected you got to understand the meaning of the dua you make, the dhikr that you make.", "Prophet Alayhi Salaam says u'idhukuma so I seek refuge in Allah or in the words of Allah, kalimatillah al tammah with the perfect words of Allah. What is this kalimatillah al tammah? Some scholars they said it's the Quran. Or it's the the qadar, the words that Allah uses to determine things. Or it's the perfect words of Allah, complete perfect words of Allah that Allah Azza Wajjal says in the Quran Qul law kana al bahru midada li kalimati Rabbi la nafida al bahru qabla an tanfada kalimatu Rabbi walaw ji'na bi mithlihi madada. If the sea was like ink so we can use to write the words of Allah these perfected words of Allah, it wouldn't be suffice even if the whole world was the sea.", "Even if you bring other seas, it wouldn't suffice the words of Allah Azza Wajjal. So these perfected words, we seek refuge in the words of Allah and it is the attribute of Allah. The of of Allah is attribute. We seek refuge in the words of Allah, perfected words of Allah, from every shaitan, min kulli shaitanin, wa hammah. Hammah is something that bites and has a poisonous bite. Let's say a scorpion, a snake. So, from every shaitan, from each shaitan and everything that is poisonous, that bite has a poisonous bite. Wa min kulli ainil lammah, from every envious eye.", "So, this hadith, au'idhukuma bi kalimatillahi tammah min kulli shaitanin wa hammah wa kulli ainil lammah, you say to protect your children. If If it's a boy, au'idhuka bi kalimatillahi tammah and the rest of the hadith. Variation. If it's a girl, au'idhuki. So, for the girl, au'idhuki. For the boy, au'idhuka. And for two, au'idhukuma. And if it's a group of children, au'idhukum bi kalimatillahi tammah. So, you would say this, which the Prophet Alaihis Salam himself would use as a protection for Hassan and Hussein. That's how you protect your family. You recite You can also recite the Mu'awwidhat.", "Qul hu Allahu Ahad, Qul a'udhu bi rabbil falaq, Qul a'udhu bi rabbin nas on your kids. At the time of of sleep, have them do wudu. Recite Ayat al-Kursi, and Qul a'udhu bi rabbil falaq, Qul a'udhu bi rabbin nas. So, after you do that, you blow and wipe over them three times, or over yourself if you're the one doing it three times as a form of protection. Cuz maybe they had an evil eye in the morning. Maybe they had sahr. Maybe they had ain. If you do this before they sleep, you are protecting your children from evil things.", "And look, when you say it, like when we recite min sharri al-waswasi al-khannas, from the evil of al-waswas, the one who whispers, al-khannas. What does that even mean? This is about understanding what I was saying, understanding what we're reciting. So, Abdullah ibn Abbas, he says, \"A shaitan, jinn or the shaitan, is staying on the heart of the son of Adam. If you mention Allah, then he does khunus.\" Khannas means that he runs away, he moves away, or he leaves. He retreats. That's why he's called al-khannas. And if you forget the remembrance of Allah, he whispers.", "So, we can be always in a state of protection from the Shaitan's whispers if we're always mentioning Allah. So, the key is this from this narration from the Abbas we can understand. The key this Shaitan Khannas that we try to protect our children and ourselves from, the more we are the as long as we're remembering Allah, he is far away, he's distant, he's retreating. The moment you forget, he will come and whisper you. So, this is how you protect your children. Now, what about protecting your house? Well, because now we know we know how to protect ourselves, we know how to protect our children.", "But, even our house? Yes, even our house. We can protect our house. How do we protect our house from evil things? First, as we said earlier in the video, when you enter the house, you say \"Bismillah Assalamualaikum.\" You mention Allah's name and you say \"Assalamualaikum.\" Then, you're sure that the jinn are not entering with you. So, you're protecting. Remove music from your house. I know some people find this difficult. But, remove music from your house if you want to protect your house. is the voice of the Shaitan. When Allah says \"Bisautika\" with with your voice referring to the Shaitan, look at the narrations that talk about music and singing.", "This is the tafsir of the Sahaba. It brings them over, brings them uh closer. It's the voice of the Shaitan. Keep constant dhikr and adhkar in the house and Quran playing, for example, or or some good dhikr or remembrance of Allah playing in the house or recited in the house. Keep it always on so you can protect your house. Recite Surah Al-Baqarah in your house because the Prophet told us the Shaitan yanfiru, he runs away or is repelled from the house that Surah Al-Baqarah is recited in. Also, don't hang pictures around the house. This this is not a thing that doesn't include the things you need for necessity or things you're keeping in drawings like your ID and stuff like that.", "We're not talking about that. We're talking about hanging pictures around your house. Don't do that. Cuz the angels don't enter. We know the Hadith, the angels don't enter a house that has pictures, images. And if the angels don't enter, then the Shaitan will enter. Don't leave crosses in your house. Now, someone come and I'll come and say, \"But what what kind of a Muslim has a cross in his house?\" We'll say that this is not referring to an actual cross, but two objects come together and crucify, like two pens, two things, two objects come come together and crucify, become a crucifix.", "So, be careful in your house that not to leave these things in your house. Cuz as Aisha reported, that the Prophet said, \"La yakruku shayan fihi tasalib illa nakada.\" The Prophet wouldn't leave anything that had any crosses in it except that he would remove it. Now, the Prophet doesn't have a cross in his house, obviously, but it's things that it becomes a cross by coming together. So, be careful from these. Also, the clothing in the house, or the kids' clothing, or the the bed coverings, or any of these things, make sure they don't have crosses or pictures.", "Same idea. Then, also understand that the house that you do qiyam al-layl in, and our night prayer in, it's protected. Cuz you have the dhikr of Allah happening in it. And the more recitation of dhikr of Allah is there, then your house will be protected. The last thing is the dogs. Shouldn't have dogs in the house. We know the hadith of the Prophet alayhi wasallam. He had an appointment with Jibreel, and Jibreel didn't come. And the Prophet alayhi wasallam did not know when he came out, and then he saw Jibreel, and then he asked him why he didn't enter.", "So, Jibreel alayhi wasallam told him because there was a dog in the house. Now, you can keep a dog in Islam, obviously, right? You can keep a dog in Islam outside the house for protection. You can use a dog for farming, you can use a dog for hunting. It's not an issue. There's no issues with dogs. They're creation of Allah. However, keeping them in the house prevents angels from entering, and you want the angels in your house so you do not have shayatin and jinn in your house. So, this is how we protect ourselves, our children, on our families from jinn, ayn, and sihr, and these things.", "We need to put these things into practices, brothers and sisters. Not just listen and hear and like, \"Okay, I understand. Now I know what what I can do so I can protect myself.\" No, you can't you need to actually implement these things. Also, if you enter into another place, let's say you enter into another location, and you want to protect yourself, the prophet Sallallahu alayhi wasallam says, Man nazala manzilan, whoever enters a place. It could be a scary place, an abandoned house, whatever, and you're afraid. Anywhere you enter, in a hotel, anything you in a place you enter.", "Faqala, say, \"A'udhu bi kalimatillahi tammat min sharri ma khalaq.\" I seek refuge in kalimatillahi, in the words of Allah. We explained what it means, right? Tammat. From the evil, from anything that Allah created. The prophet said, \"Lam yadurruhu shay'un hatta yartahila min manzilihi.\" Nothing will harm him until he leaves that place. So, if you enter another place, another house, not your house now, enter another place, if you say these words, \"A'udhu bi kalimatillahi tammat min sharri ma khalaq.\" Upon your entering, nothing will harm you until you leave that place. Now, the last thing is some people suffer from nightmares.", "How do we deal with nightmares? How do we deal with these issues? First, to protect yourself before you sleep, we mentioned, you say Ayat al- Kursi. Internalize the meaning, understand all of the things that I told you, how to protect yourself properly, these things need to be present. When you're doing the dhikr, so you you recite Ayat al-Kursi, you recite the Mu'awwidhat, and you do wudu, you do these things, and then you you wipe over yourself. As the hadith of the prophet Sallallahu alayhi wasallam says that the shaytan will not come to you until you wake up.", "Now, in the the dreams themselves, so you this is before you sleep. But the dreams the dreams themselves, it's very important. Prophet Sallallahu alayhi wasallam told us that the ru'ya, the good visions from Allah, and bad dream or nightmare is from the shaytan. Then the prophet told us, \"Idha ra'a ahadukum ma yakrah.\" If one of you sees something he dislikes, a bad nightmare, an evil dream, or whatever, fal So, you have your your left, and you do nafth, which is a form of blowing, or let's say spitting without saliva, three times. Okay? On your left here.", "On your left side. As you turn your face and you do it with on your left side. And then You seek refuge in Allah from the shaitan. You say \"A'udhu billahi min ash-shaitan ir-rajim.\" And from what you saw three times. Then you switch and sleep on the other side or sleep or switch to the other side. Because it will not harm him. If you do this, it will not harm you. But there is a very important point here. Wala yukhbir ahadan. Not to say to anyone what you saw. Now, many people see bad dreams. You wake up.", "Right next to you your husband and you start telling him what happened. We have the narration of the Prophet Muhammad who said he saw he saw like his head rolling and he was running behind his head. So, Prophet Muhammad told him Do not let one of you speak about the shaitan manipulation of him. This is shaitan manipulating you. Do not speak about it. Many people see bad dreams and come oh shaikh or scholar this and that. I saw this and that and that. I don't know what what's the explanation. If it's a bad dream, do not tell anyone.", "Why? What is the wisdom? Because the shaitan is manipulating you. He's he's playing games with you. So, if you go and tell the people he's happy. However, if you don't say, then that is frustrating. Because the point of the shaitan manipulating you or making fun of you, he's like you kept silent, you didn't say anything. It's like imagine someone is mocking you. You don't speak about it. You ignore it. You don't do anything. It's frustrating. So, you do not speak about that. That is one of the cures from these things. Don't go around speaking to people doing this.", "But this is what you do. And I already know. Like many of us don't even know that this is a practice that you do if you see something bad. And many of us, even if the ones who know, they don't do it. So, if you want protection, if you have nightmares, you're suffering, this is what you do. If you see something you do the blowing or the spitting without saliva on your left three times. You say \"A'udhu billahi min ash-shaitan ir-rajim.\" And \"A'udhu billahi from what you saw\" three times. And then you switch to the other side.", "And not say anything to anyone. And I ask Allah Azza Wajjal, inshallah, that we actually implement these things into our life. We actually start implementing them as a form of protection. And I ask Allah Azza Wajjal to protect all of us because all of us, any of us, could be harmed from this world of the jinn that lives with us. Nobody is like invincible. Allah is a protector. That's why we're following these measurements that are found in the Quran and Sunnah that protects us. And remember I gave you this story about this lady that accepted Islam and her daughter.", "The people who are not believers, they don't have this guidance from Allah. And many of them are suffering. Many of them experience evil things. If only they knew the guidance, they would have been Muslims. And we have the guidance, but we're not implementing it. So, inshallah, after watching this, we're actually going to start implementing it into our lives. And not just hearing something and like, you know, for the sake of hearing it. May Allah Azza Wajjal bless you and protect you all. Assalamualaikum warahmatullahi wabarakatuh.",))
#source("Source: The Muslim Lantern, \"How To Protect Yourself From Jinn, Possession, Magic & The Evil Eye In Islam - Muhammed Ali\"")

