#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("It's a long process. Obviously, Islam, unlike any other faith and religion is very descriptive of the events that take place. The afterlife, the moment you die all of that is very descriptive in the Quran and Hadith and there's a plethora of different traditions that talk about that. For example, Islam will give you, from the moment your soul is leaving your body if you're a disbeliever, the angels will come. The angels will rip the soul out of the body of the person. That would be a very painful process because the person is a disbeliever, his soul will try to hide, run in his body not to be pulled by these angels.", "Those angels will punish that person. And then when the soul is ripped out of that person's body they will come with a cloth they will descend with a group of people that are angels of.. basically for the disbeliever, angels of hellfire they bring a cloth that is dark and with a very bad odour. Then they will put that person in then that person will go down, then that person will be in the grave which is a separate life, we call it: The life of the Barzakh (بَرْزَخ: barrier or intermediate realm between this world and the Hereafter) A door of Paradise will be opened and then that disbeliever will see the door, and then he will be told, \"This would have been your seat\" \"but you'll never see this again in your life\" and then that will be closed.", "and then a door of hellfire will open and the heat and the bad odours of hellfire will be there and he'll be punished in his grave. When he's placed in the grave, the minute he's punished The grave will tighten, and his ribs will change location Because it will tighten with him. Now, there is a plethora, as I said, of descriptions. Now, for the believers, the exact opposite They will come with a white cloth with the scent of musk That person will be welcomed, he will go to Paradise A door of Paradise will be opened The scent will be there, the grave will be widened It will be