// T ML284 1010,1011,1012,1013,1014,1015,1016,1017,1018,1019,1020,1021,1022,1023,1024,1025,1026,1027,1028,1029,1030,1031,1032,1033,1034,1035,1036,1037,1038,1039,1040,1041,1042,1043,1044,1045,1046,1047,1048,1049,1050,1051,1052,1053,1054,1055,1056 | The Muslim Lantern | dash: | cut:0
#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("Belief in the Last Day, because when you believe in the Last Day and you read the descriptions of Hellfire, and you read the descriptions of Jannah (Paradise), you wouldn't be daring to do the things that you do. You wouldn't dare to transgress against the Maharim of Allahﷻ, (against the Boundaries of Allahﷻ) Because you understand what are the consequences of doing that. They say, \"you know what..\" There is the example that a friend told me once and it's a beautiful example, because it fits into this idea he said: \"If you know your Boss..\" Do you go to work, you have a boss?", "If the boss is lenient, you slack on the job, you go here and there for a few hours, you eat and drink, you're not working properly But if you know your boss is a guy who's like; if he sees anything wrong he's going to fire you, you behave accordingly, right? You'll be like this on the job! So, If you do not know ولِلّه المَثَلُ الأَعلى (for Allah is the highest of examples) there is no comparison obviously, but if you don't know Allah.. what you know of Allah; is how you're going to behave So, those people, the only thing they know about Allahﷻ, is what?", "He is Merciful, if your sins reach the sky, all of these things.. You know, \"Compassionate\" Imams today that tell compassion every day, day and night compassion only is nothing else in the Deen (Religion) of Allah Muslims have absorbed this. And based on that, they think Allah is only Merciful.. Do whatever you like! But if they were to understand that Allahﷻ in the Quran for a حِكمَة for a عِلَّة, for a reason, in multiple verses not one, He gathers punishment and reward together ٱعْلَمُوٓا۟ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ شَدِيدُ ٱلْعِقَابِ وَأَنَّ ٱللَّهَ غَفُورٌۭ رَّحِيمٌۭ Just one verse! (alMaida5:98) One verse just telling you these two things together so you understand: أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ شَدِيدُ ٱلْعِقَابِ (Allah is Severe in punishment), وَأَنَّ ٱللَّهَ غَفُورٌۭ رَّحِيمٌۭ (And Allah is Forgiving and Merciful).", "Don't take one and leave the other Do what Sheikh alislam Ibn alQayyim said: \"Muslim is like a bird, he has two wings; Hope and Fear, you're in the middle If you lean too much into one, it's a problem, if you lean too much into the other it's a problem. Of course! Not everything is fear also you can not despair from Allah's Mercy إِنَّهُۥ لَا یَا۟یۡـَٔسُ مِن رَّوۡحِ ٱللَّهِ إِلَّا ٱلۡقَوۡمُ ٱلۡكَـٰفِرُونَ (Yusuf12:87) Only the disobedient, disbelieving people are the ones who despair from Allah's Mercy completely We don't despair from Allah's Mercy, but at the same time we know that Allah has boundaries and those boundaries are to be respected, and we have to do our best and this is how we obtain Allah's Mercy.", "OK? You believe in the Last Day, you understand the Last Day, the حساب (Accountability) the موقف (Standing before Allah) What's going to happen to me when I stand before Allah? The قنطرة (Bridge)? What is this the قنطرة? What is the صراط (Path)? What is going to happen when I walk there? These things when you visualise it, when you put in your mind as a Muslim; Your behavior becomes in accordance to What You Know..",))
