 yourself, it teaches you to have discipline, when you wake up in the morning - Because one of our prayers are at dawn.", "We pray at dawn, the time of dawn, we pray a prayer called فجر, Fajr Prayer literally means: dawn So, the Fajr prayer is at the time of dawn, so it's early in the morning! depending on the sun when dawn is. But like now it's 4:30a.m, 4:20, 4:10 something like that, so, you wake up at that time to pray, so it teaches you discipline: To put God first in your life! Sleeping is very beautiful! I like sleeping! but God comes first! That's why the call of prayer that we do in Fajr time is very unique, the call of prayer at Fajr time is unique from all of the other ones, It has an extra thing it says الصلاة خير من النوم (Prayer is better than sleeping), this is the only…, this part is only in the Fajr time, It's only in the dawn prayer, it's not in the other prayers, because it's Unique to that, because that prayer is…,", "It's a prayer that teaches you discipline, also the prayer teaches you to completely eliminate racism and that's something that many religions struggle with! In certain Churches you find the Irish Church, black Church, White Church, African Church, In Islam everyone prays in the same Mosque! and when you pray; you have your feet next to other person's feet, And your shoulder next to the other person's shoulder. So you cannot be looking at that person with any type of racism; That he's less than you, you have to stand next to him, you have to put your shoulder to the shoulder, you have to put your feet to his feet, You have to stand with him for 5 times a day, you have to meet that individual, you speak to him, and he speaks to him, You say سلام (which is greetings of peace to one another).", "So; he completely eliminates racism, that's why you will find people, Or I would say the people who struggled a lot with racism like for example: Malcolm X, if you guys know Malcolm X, Or Muhammad Ali Clay the boxer, so those people struggled with racism back then Because it was very prevalent in America and many other places, and they became Muslims, And if you read the book of Malcolm X he said: when he went to pilgrimage, he saw that the only religion that is eliminating racism is Islam! He said it was the only place where he felt that everyone is the same!", "everyone is wearing the same clothes, Everyone is doing the same action, there's no difference between you based on your color and your race, Also Islam teaches you to humble yourself, it does not matter if I'm the janitor or I am the the CEO of the company, We're all standing in the same line, and what raises you in rank is your religious beliefs, So if you memories more of the Quran; you will lead the prayer, So if I'm the janitor, I memorize more Quran than you, Islamically, I will lead the prayer! even though you're the CEO you're going to stand behind me!", "Because it's not about the worldly levels of where you are, it's about your connection with God, So it teaches you to humble yourself, and not to belittle others and look down upon them, I obviously; the prayers are…, so many things I can go on and say the benefits of the prayer, But that's why the prayer for us as Muslims is the most essential act a human being can do, OK?",))
