#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("Well the Prophetﷺ told us the thing is, if someone sleeps, the Prophetﷺ he said: مَنْ نامَ عَنْ صَلاةٍ أو نَسِيَها فَلْيُصَلِّها إِذا ذَكَرَها (whoever sleeps on a prayer or forgets about it, he prays it whenever he remembers it) So the minute you remember you pray. The Prophetﷺ made the exceptions there, these are the exceptions: You forget about the prayer or you sleep and you miss the prayer. But there is a condition there in the sleeping The condition in the sleeping is that you're putting effort to wake up, meaning I'm trying to sleep as much as early as I can I know my schedule, I know what works with me.", "Find someone sleeping like 30 minutes before the prayer, that person is sinning 100%, because he waited all that time, and that 30 minutes he slept instead of praying. So it doesn't work there. The condition for you to not be held accountable; is that you try your best. You sleep as early as you can, you leave the alarm, if you know someone who can wake you up, you tell them to wake you up, you're taking all the means. If you did that, Allah knows your intention – If you tried, and you couldn't do it then as the Prophetﷺ said you..",))
