#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("Yeah I'll tell you.. Of course I miss the prayer sometimes and the reason being, for example let's say I'm travelling and I might spend like.. I travel to a different country the plane was six hours and then I reach there towards 12 o'clock and فجر (Fajr: the morning prayer) is like 4 o'clock So it's not like I slept late but I came from the travel and I slept, and I was so tired that I could not stay awake for four more hours Obviously I just came from travel so I slept. But due to the tiredness, even though I put the alarm and try my best, I couldn't wake up because I was so tired, I missed that prayer.", "So then, I pray it when I wake up The Prophetﷺ himself he missed a prayer you know, so let alone everyone else The Prophetﷺ was with his Companions, and it was also the morning prayer, and they were travelling and on the way, they put one person to stay awake one of the Companions of the Prophetﷺ The Prophet said you stay awake and wake us up. OK? And the rest of the people went to sleep. That person who was supposed to stay awake he slept, he couldn't stay awake as he was told, So he slept and everyone also continued to sleep, and the Prophetﷺ said because they are travelling, they were very tired, they only woke up from the heat of the sun, you know the sun is now burning it's too hot so they wake up.", "And then the Prophetﷺ prayed that prayer with everyone that they missed, and he didn't say anything because he knows that person was tired in the travel and all of that and he tried to stay awake but he slept. So we're all human. No one is perfect Don't think that there would be me or someone who's you know a record of perfect score, there's nothing..",))
