=== 14.4 Abandoning the prayer
// NODE P02.C08.S04
// EXCERPT ML284 465-578
// T ML284 465,466,467,468,469,470,471,472,473,474,475,476,477,478,479,480,481,482,483,484,485,486,487,488,489,490,491,492,493,494,495,496,497,498,499,500,501,502,503,504,505,506,507,508,509,510,511,512,513,514,515,516,517,518,519,520,521,522,523,524,525,526,527,528,529,530,531,532,533,534,535,536,537,538,539,540,541,542,543,544,545,546,547,548,549,550,551,552,553,554,555,556,557,558,559,560,561,562,563,564,565,566,567,568,569,570,571,572,573,574,575,576,577,578 | The Muslim Lantern | dash: | cut:0
#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("Now we have also the Fitna of Shahawat, of desires, we mentioned two types Now the Fitna of Desires.. What is the most common sin that we see today? The most important among them is what?.. The Prayer! Muslims do not pray. The Prayer that Allahﷻ have made عمادُ الدين (The pillar of this religion), the religion of Islam The pillar of this religion that the Prophetﷺ have made the differentiator between believer and disbeliever What differentiates a Believer from a Disbeliever is the prayer! This most important foundational thing in Islam.. Muslims are not fulfilling anymore! Come to the Masjid (Mosque) it's empty.", "you see Eid عيد there's no place in the street to stand! So there is this number of Muslims. They exist. These people are Muslims They come to pray Eid unless (Kuffar: Disbelievers) they come to pray Eid with us or something! It's the same Muslims, right? Your Uncle, Brother, Sister. These are the people who are coming to pray for Eid So why is that the same group of people are praying this prayer Eid or Jumu'a جُمُعة -which is a less number of people- Less people coming but still many people do come. Why don't we see them in the rest of the prayers?", "Why we don't see them in the Masjid, when it's time to pray? Why is it only in the Eid prayer? The simple happy, you know holidays, money, dancing is OK. But when it comes to Salah the rest of the year, no? Or Ramadan, you see the Masjid is full. And some people use this term Ramadan Muslims -Even though I don't agree with it- If someone comes to Allah in Ramadan, Alhamdulillah (Praise is due to God), but they use that term for a reason, The term comes for what reason? Is the fact that you see these people only in Ramadan and you don't see them the rest of the year, that's why they use that term \"Ramadan Muslims\", because the fact is you only see them in Ramadan, So it's like the guy who only comes to you in a specific holiday, he becomes a \"person of the Holiday\", isn't it?", "Some relatives that only see you in Eid, some of the relatives you only see them in Eid. So it's a Holiday Person, that's why they started saying \"Ramadan Muslim\". So this prayer.. That is what a lot of Muslims don't understand and they need to keep in mind, and they need to understand, is the Prophetﷺ said: العَهْدُ الذّي بينَنا وبينَهم الصلاةُ (The difference between the believer and the disbeliever, is الصلاة Prayer) فمَن تركَها فقد كفرَ (Who leaves it, has committed disbelief) Prophetﷺ said.. Look! this is not my words, I want you to pay attention, this is the speech of the Prophetﷺ Before you tell me \"but it means this\", did the prophet say it means this or that?", "Or is this the end of the Hadith? This is the end of the Hadith. Did the prophet explain this in another Hadith? No, this is the statement that the prophetﷺ said, I'm saying to you the same statement the prophetﷺ said. If you say to me, you can not say this without explaining it, how come the prophetﷺ say it without explaining it, then? How come the prophetﷺ said it without explaining what it means according to your understanding? He said it like it is, He said: إنَّ بيْنَ الرَّجُلِ وبيْنَ الشِّرْكِ والْكُفْرِ (Between the servant of Allah and Polytheism and Disbelief) is what?", "تَرْكَ الصَّلاةِ (Leaving the prayer) فَمن تَركَها فقَد كفَر (Who leaves it he commit disbelief) Between the عبد between the servant of Allah and leaving the prayer.. الشرك والكفر becoming a Kafir (Disbeliever), becoming a Mushrik (Polytheist), is leaving the prayer! Someone comes, but the 'Ulama later on they said this, and they said that, brother they said this.. OK, brother there are reports we have from the التابعين (atTabi'in: Followers).. They said reporting consensus Complete agreement, upon the Sahaba that the person who completely abandons the prayer is a disbeliever Some people pray sometimes, and leave sometimes, pray Jumu'a, pray Eid, I'm not talking about these people I'm saying someone completely abandons the prayer and doesn't pray anymore at all, it's been 1 year he's never prayed, 6 months, 7 month, 8 months, few Eids they passed by, they have not prayed, now the Tabi'i what did he say?", "He says: كانَ أَصْحابُ مُحَمَّدٍﷺ (The Companions of Prophet Muhammadﷺ) they did not see anything as disbelief, they did not see any action that you leave it, is disbelief, except the Prayer! You have 'Umar Ibn al Khattab saying -and many of the Sahaba! I'll just mention what 'Umar said- He said: لاَ حَظَّ فِي الإِسْلاَمِ (there's no portion of Islam) لِمَنْ تَرَكَ الصَّلاَةَ (for whoever leaves the Prayer) Now someone comes to you and says: The 'Ulama later on they said, that means he does جحود (Juhood). You know what Juhood means? Juhood means that he says: \"I do not believe I have to pray, it's not an obligation in Islam to pray\", They say this is what the prophet means.", "Did the Prophet say Juhood in the Hadith? No! But they say to you that the 'Ulama, the مذاهب (Madhahib: Schools of Thoughts), and they attribute certain things to ashShafi'i, and Malik, which are not as they attribute it. But they say this is how we understand it. And they say to you \"The majority of the schools of thought..\" -and it's true, the majority of the later Scholars after the Sahaba already agreed based on the statement that we mentioned- The later Scholars many of them have said it is Juhood, and it means to deny that the prayer is an obligation, but we say to them, the Tabi'i he said, \"leaving an action\", he didn't say an action that you leave..", "Not you do Juhood of, but you leave.. There's no actions that you leave necessarily and you become a disbeliever, but you do Juhood of; that means you say it's not an obligation But we say no problem, let's accept your opinion -because they would say to us you're going to call the majority of the Ummah disbelievers- You want to take the opinion of the people -which is the opinion I don't take personally- but you want to take the opinion of the 'Ulama who said: It's actually Juhood. So if he leaves it out of laziness, he's not a disbeliever.", "So only if he believes he doesn't have to pray We say OK, you know, the most lenient opinion among these opinions, is the opinion of Abu Hanifa anNu'man, the Hanafi School of Thought Do you know what that opinion says? If that person doesn't pray, he's put in Prison He's going to be put in Prison, and be told to pray, to repent and Pray. You need to Pray. So this is the most lenient opinion, if you want to take the most lenient opinion, at least follow it, follow the most lenient opinion You don't want to take the opinion that it is a disbelief, then take the most lenient opinion and show us the implementation of the opinion So this pillar of Islam, Allah said in the Quran, He mentioned the description of أنبياء (Anbiya': Prophets), and then He said (Maryam19:59) فَخَلَفَ مِنۢ بَعۡدِهِمۡ خَلۡفٌ (And then they came after them a generation)", "أَضَاعُوا۟ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ (They wasted the prayer) وَٱتَّبَعُوا۟ ٱلشَّهَوَ ٰ⁠تِۖ.. -The Fitna of Shahawat!- (They followed their desires) فَسَوۡفَ یَلۡقَوۡنَ غَیًّا (Then they certainly will have غيّ), and غيّ (Ghay) is the liquid that comes from the people of Hellfire, you know the liquid that comes out of them.. That person will drink it –according to 'Abdullah Ibn 'Abbas– Allahﷻ says in the Quran (alMa'un107:4) فَوَیۡلࣱ لِّلۡمُصَلِّینَ (So woe be to those who pray) Let alone people who don't pray, yes? فَوَیۡلࣱ لِّلۡمُصَلِّینَ (Woe be to..) And \"Woe\" here, 'Abdullah Ibn 'Abbas says: It is a Valley in جهنم (Jahannam: Hellfire).", "And then the other opinion that it is وعيدٌ شديد it is a (very harsh warning) from Allahﷻ He says to those who pray, pray sometimes, and leave some prayers, or delay the prayers until the time comes out, or all.. Or any of these things, but \"they pray\", so imagine the person who doesn't pray at all! But you have the Muslims today leaving completely their Prayer, they don't Pray, they leave the Prayer",))
