#other("Clip", ("The آذان (Adhan: Call to prayer) on a Friday.. Bid'ah! Uthmanؓ رَضِيَ ٱللَّٰهُ عَنْهُ (Radiya Allahu 'anhu: May Allah be pleased with him) innovated this great innovation and that is a good Bid'ah",))
// T ML285 136,137,138,139,140,141,142,143,144,145,146,147,148,149,150,151,152,153,154,155,156,157,158,159,160,161,162,163,164,165,166,167,168,169,170,171,172,173,174,175,176,177,178,179,180,181,182,183,184,185,186,187,188,189 | The Muslim Lantern | dash: | cut:0
#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("He says Uthmanؓ innovated this Good Bid'aah. Did Uthmanؓ call this action a Bid'ah? Did he say, \"I'm doing a good Bid'ah\"? Did Uthmanؓ innovate the Adhan? Or is the Adhan something that existed from the time of the Prophetﷺ? Is there also an instance of the Prophetﷺ making Adhan twice for a specific reason? For example, for Fajr, there were two Adhans, an early Adhan and then an Adhan afterwards The Prophetﷺ used to say to Abdullah ibn Maktum to do an Adhan and then Bilal did the Adhan for Fajr So there is an early Adhan there.. and still there.", "If you go to Mecca, there's the first Adhan and the second Adhan The Prophetﷺ did it, so there's two types of Adhan there. It's not only that the Adhan is a part of Islam, but there was for a specific reason.. The Prophetﷺ has commanded two Adhans, like the one early for Fajr to wake the people up and the second is for the prayer So the جمعة (Jumaa: Friday prayer) here.. Uthmanؓ, when he said to do the Adhan twice, what was the reason? It is explained in the same narration that talks about Uthmanؓ introducing the other Adhan.", "It mentions the reason It says that the reason was that Islam has spread and religion has spread everywhere and then there were many many people, So if you do one Adhan, people do not have enough time to reach the Masjid, they're far away So he used to send someone to the market and he does the Adhan there or he does the إِقَامَة (Iqamah: Second call to prayer) there, So that the people can be alerted that this is the time of the prayer and they can have enough time to come So, you cannot come and say, \"This is a Bid'ah Hasana\", as if Uthmanؓ was saying \"This is a Bid'ah\" And the thing is this: Anything that Abu Bakrؓ did or Umar ibn al-Khattab does..", "or Ali.. or Uthman.. Anything that these four people do is by default sanctioned and given legitimacy by the Prophetﷺ. Why? Because the Prophetﷺ said in the Hadith: فعليكم بسنتي وسنة الخلفاء الراشدين المهديين من بعدي (Upon you is my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly guided Khulafa arrashideen who will come after me) \"The guided Khulafa\" (plural of Khalifa: Caliph, a Successor Ruler to the Prophet) they're guided. The Prophetﷺ said to follow their Sunnah So, if I follow the Sunnah of Uthman, I'm following the Prophetﷺ, and I've got the origin there Because the Prophetﷺ said these people are special people, you follow their Sunnah.", "They're not like everyone else Did the Prophetﷺ tell you that you are from the Khulafa arrashideen and we should follow your Sunnah today? Is that the reason? No! it is very simple. Those Khulafa al-Rashideen have a specific authority given by the Prophetﷺ that they are guided And they are the closest Companions to the Prophetﷺ. They are the best people in this أُمَّةُ (Ummah: Muslim Nation) And they have been given the authority and we've been commanded to follow their Sunnah. What they do, we can do, OK? Even if you assume that this is a new action, it's not like it already existed..", "the Adhan existed at the time of the Prophet Even if you assume that this is a new action and it was not done only for that specific reason, that the people are far away and they were not reaching.. Even if you want to ignore all of this, we still have evidence there that the Prophetﷺ said that we can follow Uthmanؓ His Sunnah, what he does. We can follow his Sunnah. So, we have an evidence where we can follow Uthmanؓ In what he did, which is the second Adhan. So you have no evidence there. Let's see the second example",))
