#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("Again, did 'Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz say, \"This is a Bid'ah\"? And did he say, \"This is a good Bid'aah -innovation- that I've innovated\"? You attribute things to the Sahaba and the Salaf Assalih that they've not said You put it in their mouth and you say, \"This is a good Bid'ah\". They didn't say that it's a good Bid'ah Now, he said \"minarets\". Look, that's the reason I identified for you and I explained to you in the beginning of the video what is a Bid'ah The reason I explained this is because you have people like this They bring something like a building, a structure, and they say this is a Bid'ah.", "Is this a part of the religion? Isn't this what I told you already? A وسيلة (means) for us to do a specific thing, like the Adhan, for the Adhan, we use this as a means Like I'm using this microphone as a means and the camera as a means to reach you We use this minaret as a means to reach more people. They were using it so the voice can reach more people And the مُؤَذِّن (Muadhin: caller of Adhan) at the time of the Prophetﷺ used to find the highest place in the ground and they go up and they do the Adhan Like Bilal used to go on top of the Ka'aba (Cubic building, House of God and Prayer's Direction) or they go on top of a mountain and they do the Adhan Because when you are in a high place, then that sound reaches other people", "This would be similar like saying that the microphone is a Bid'ah, internet.. everything is a Bid'ah According to this person, everything literally is going to be a Bid'ah. If building something is a Bid'ah, Then everything is going to be a Bid'ah based on this idea and understanding",))
