#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("OK, so you see here.. Here now, he said that \"the Sahabi have said it\", he said his statement.. But other people, he attributed to them that this is a Good Bid'ah because none of them have said that it's a Good Bid'ah But 'Umar ibn al-Khattabؓ, he says he said it. Look, he said that it's a good Bid'aah. He said what means that it's a good Bid'aah So, you agree that in this case, you have a statement But in the other situations, you literally put that statement in the mouth of those people because none of them have said what you said Now, praying Taraweeh in Jam'aa is a Bid'aah?", "There is a Hadith of the Prophetﷺ where he prayed Taraweeh And he gathered the people and he led them in Jam'aa, and he didn't do it for one night, he did it for multiple nights And the Hadith mentions the Prophetﷺ doing it, and the Hadith also mentions the Prophetﷺ left it. For what reason? He left it because he said: I am afraid it's going to become an obligation on you. If I continue to do it, it will become obligatory and everyone will have to pray Taraweeh It's not going to be a Sunnah, it's going to be an obligatory action, so the Prophet left it for that reason When the Prophetﷺ died and the time of 'Umar ibn alkhattab came, he said \"OK, I'm going to gather the people again now\" Remember what I said to you in the beginning?", "When the Sahaba say \"Bid'ah Hasana\", they are referring to an action That the Prophetﷺ did that the people have forgotten and left, an action that people are no longer doing So you bring it back, which already has an origin in the Sharia. So, this is what 'Umar ibn Alkhattab did He brought an action that the Prophetﷺ already did and he led the people in Jam'aa because now it cannot become an obligation Because the Prophetﷺ died. So, no Shar' (Law), no revelation is going to come and say now it's an obligation Now, you want to say \"Bid'ah\"..", "This is something the Prophetﷺ literally did himself and he led the people and there is an explicit Hadith I think these people know these things. They're telling you these things but with the intention -most of the time-.. I don't know this person, but generally, most of them, they do this with the intention to deceive you They already know the answers, they already know the Prophetﷺ did this, But they just say it for the sake of misusing it, telling the lay people that they do not know the Prophetﷺ did it, so they tell the people these types of things",))
